  "Breadboard rows follow the image letters: the visual top half is rows f-j (catalogue bank 'b'), the visual bottom half is rows a-e (bank 't').",
  "Column positions were estimated from the image. The 4.7K resistor appears to sit in columns 22-24 in the image, but it must share the photoresistor/A0 node, so I placed it at 21t.c to 24t.c.",
  "The parts list says 6 hook-up wires, but the image shows 5 wires (red 5V, black GND, blue A0, blue pin 9, and a black one from the speaker). I treated the black one as the speaker's own lead going straight to the Arduino GND pin next to AREF (GND.1). I used 4 jumper-wire parts and no extra sixth wire.",
  "Resistor values are 100 ohm (speaker series) and 4.7K (pull-down). The schematic mislabels the speaker resistor as 10K, but the manual text and parts list say 100 ohm. The resistor catalogue type has a value prop, so I set value=100 and value=4700."
